---
import '@fontsource-variable/roboto-serif';
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import { rates, gbp } from '../data/rates';
import { testimonialsFor } from '../data/testimonials';
import { faqsFor } from '../data/faqs';
import FaqList from '../components/FaqList.astro';

const TURNSTILE_SITEKEY = '0x4AAAAAAEcCwzuExy2fSCmH';

const testimonials = testimonialsFor('fractional');
const fractionalFaqs = faqsFor('fractional');

const serviceSchema = {
  '@type': 'Service',
  '@id': 'https://intentionaut.com/fractional/#service',
  name: 'Fractional & Interim Product Leadership',
  serviceType: 'Fractional product leadership',
  description:
    'Director-level product leadership for a defined period: one or two days a week, three months and up, with executive stakeholder access and accountability for delivery.',
  provider: { '@id': 'https://intentionaut.com/#person' },
  areaServed: { '@type': 'Country', name: 'United Kingdom' },
  offers: {
    '@type': 'Offer',
    priceCurrency: 'GBP',
    price: rates.fractional,
    unitText: 'day',
    availability: 'https://schema.org/LimitedAvailability',
  },
};

const faqSchema = {
  '@type': 'FAQPage',
  mainEntity: fractionalFaqs.map((f) => ({
    '@type': 'Question',
    name: f.question,
    acceptedAnswer: { '@type': 'Answer', text: f.answer.replace(/\s+/g, ' ').trim() },
  })),
};
---

<BaseLayout
  title="Fractional & Interim Product Leadership | Saielle DaSilva"
  description="Fractional and interim product leadership for teams that need a senior product owner now, not a permanent hire yet: Director-level direction, decisions and delivery for a defined period."
  jsonLd={[serviceSchema, faqSchema]}
  ogImage="/og/fractional.png"
>
  <section class="wrap">
    <header class="page-head">
      <p class="eyebrow">Leadership &amp; advisory</p>
      <h1>A senior product leader without the permanent commitment.</h1>
      <p class="lede">
        For teams that need Director-level leadership, but are not ready for
        a permanent hire.
      </p>
      <ul class="problem-lines">
        <li>A product that works and nobody likes, with no agreement on why.</li>
        <li>Designers with nobody senior leading them.</li>
        <li>AI features where nobody can yet say what good looks like.</li>
      </ul>
    </header>

    <div class="prose">
      <p>
        Sometimes you do not need a consultant. You need someone who will
        own the problem. Someone who shows up, makes the hard calls,
        leads the team and stays accountable for the outcome.
      </p>
      <p>
        But the timing is not right for a permanent hire. The role is
        evolving. You need to prove the model before you commit. Or you
        need someone senior while you figure out the permanent answer.
      </p>

      <h2>What I do</h2>
      <p>
        I become your senior product leader for a defined period. Typically
        one or two days a week, over three to six months. I have executive
        stakeholder access, I lead the team, I make strategic decisions and
        I am accountable for delivery.
      </p>
      <p>
        This is not advisory from the sidelines. It is leadership from
        inside the organisation, with the same authority and accountability
        as a permanent Director.
      </p>

      <h2>What you get</h2>
      <ul>
        <li>Strategic decisions and product direction</li>
        <li>Team leadership and coaching</li>
        <li>Product operating model design and run</li>
        <li>Executive stakeholder management</li>
        <li>Delivery accountability and outcomes</li>
      </ul>

      <h2>How it works</h2>
      <p>
        A minimum commitment of three months. One or two days a week. Enough
        time to build context, lead with authority and create real momentum.
      </p>
      <p>
        The engagement ends with a clear handover: a functioning team, an
        operating model that runs without me, and decisions that do not need
        relitigating.
      </p>
      <p>
        Sometimes what is missing is not direction but a working version of the
        idea, quickly. That is
        {' '}<a href="/forward-deployed/">forward deployed product building</a>:
        three days a week in your environment, four weeks and up, building
        rather than leading.
      </p>

      <h2>Where I have done this</h2>
      <p>
        As interim CPO at a direct-to-consumer grocery scaleup, monthly
        recurring revenue grew 450 per cent in 90 days. I led the product and
        design organisation at StepStone, where the satellite portfolio
        returned 3.2x. At Sainsbury's I ran product for AI, data platforms and
        machine learning, and took production AI from a handful of experiments
        to a platform serving over 100 million customers. I was on the founding
        team at Cazoo, through to a $7B IPO.
      </p>
      {testimonials.map((t) => (
        <figure class="frac-quote">
          <blockquote><p>{t.quote}</p></blockquote>
          <figcaption>
            {t.url ? <a href={t.url} target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">{t.name}</a> : t.name},
            {' '}{t.role}, {t.org}
          </figcaption>
        </figure>
      ))}

      <h2>How to start</h2>
      <p>
        A free preliminary call. We check it is a fit. If it is, you get a
        written proposal: what we would do, when, and what it costs.
      </p>
      <p>
        Need a second opinion rather than a leader? That is the
        {' '}<a href="/contact/">strategy session</a>: {gbp(rates.strategySession)},
        90 minutes, on its own, separate from fractional work.
      </p>
    </div>

    <section class="contact-form-section" aria-label="Get in touch">
      <div class="contact-card">
        <h2>Let's talk.</h2>
        <p class="form-lede">
          If your team needs a senior product leader who will own the problem
          and stay until it is solved, let us talk.
        </p>
        <form id="contact-form" novalidate>
          <input type="hidden" name="source" value="fractional" />
          <div class="form-grid">
            <label>
              <span class="form-label">Name</span>
              <input type="text" name="name" required autocomplete="name" />
            </label>
            <label>
              <span class="form-label">Email</span>
              <input type="email" name="email" required autocomplete="email" />
            </label>
          </div>
          <label>
            <span class="form-label">What's this about?</span>
            <select name="topic">
              <option value="forward-deployed">Forward deployed product building</option>
              <option value="advisor-intro">Advisor or recruiter introduction</option>
              <option value="strategic-direction">
                Strategic direction
              </option>
              <option value="execution">Execution &amp; transformation</option>
              <option value="fractional" selected>
                Fractional leadership
              </option>
              <option value="advisory">Advisory</option>
              <option value="speaking">Speaking &amp; workshops</option>
              <option value="mentoring">Mentoring</option>
              <option value="other">Something else</option>
            </select>
          </label>
          <label>
            <span class="form-label">Message</span>
            <textarea name="message" rows="5" required></textarea>
          </label>
          {
            TURNSTILE_SITEKEY && (
              <>
                <div
                  class="cf-turnstile"
                  data-sitekey={TURNSTILE_SITEKEY}
                  data-theme="light"
                />
                <script
                  is:inline
                  src="https://challenges.cloudflare.com/turnstile/v0/api.js"
                  async
                  defer
                />
              </>
            )
          }
          <button class="btn-plain" type="submit">Send it</button>
          <p class="form-status" id="form-status" role="status"></p>
        </form>
      </div>
      <p class="faq-link">
        Questions first? <a href="/faq/">Read the FAQ.</a>
      </p>
    </section>

    <FaqList
      items={fractionalFaqs}
      sub="What founders ask before bringing in a part-time leader."
    />
  </section>

  <script>
    const ENDPOINT = 'https://contact-form.intentionaut.workers.dev/contact';
    const form = document.getElementById('contact-form');

    form?.addEventListener('submit', async (e) => {
      e.preventDefault();
      const data = Object.fromEntries(new FormData(form));
      const statusEl = document.getElementById('form-status');

      try {
        const res = await fetch(ENDPOINT, {
          method: 'POST',
          headers: { 'Content-Type': 'application/json' },
          body: JSON.stringify(data),
        });
        const result = await res.json();
        if (res.ok) {
          form.reset();
          if (statusEl) statusEl.textContent = result.message || "Thank you; I'll reply soon.";
        } else {
          if (statusEl) statusEl.textContent = result.error || 'Something went wrong; please email me directly.';
        }
      } catch {
        if (statusEl) statusEl.textContent = 'Something went wrong; please email me directly.';
      }
    });
  </script>
</BaseLayout>

<style>
  .frac-quote {
    margin: var(--space-6) 0;
  }
  .frac-quote blockquote {
    margin: 0;
  }
  .frac-quote blockquote p {
    margin: 0;
  }
  .frac-quote figcaption {
    margin-top: var(--space-3);
    padding-left: var(--space-6);
    font-size: 0.9rem;
    color: var(--muted);
  }
</style>
